{name:"One Pan Chicken & Rice",category:"Family",tags:["Budget","High Protein","One Pan"],time:40,cost:1.82,protein:38,calories:612,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.4,emoji:"🍗",blurb:"Golden chicken, smoky rice and one pan to wash. Even you can manage that.",ingredients:["600g chicken thighs","300g long-grain rice","1 red pepper, sliced","1 onion, diced","750ml chicken stock","2 tsp smoked paprika","150g frozen peas"],steps:["Season and brown the chicken in a deep pan for 6 minutes.","Soften the onion and pepper, then stir in rice and paprika.","Pour in stock, return the chicken, cover and simmer for 22 minutes.","Stir through peas for the final 4 minutes. Rest before serving — patience, hero."]},
{name:"Sausage Pasta Bake",category:"Family",tags:["Budget","Batch Cook"],time:45,cost:1.95,protein:31,calories:694,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.2,emoji:"🍝",blurb:"A bubbling tray of sausage, tomato and cheese. Beige food done properly.",ingredients:["8 pork sausages","350g penne","500g passata","1 onion, diced","2 garlic cloves","150g grated mozzarella","1 tsp oregano"],steps:["Brown the sausages, slice them, and try not to eat half.","Boil pasta for 2 minutes less than the packet says.","Cook onion and garlic, add passata, oregano and sausage.","Mix with pasta, cover with cheese and bake at 200°C for 20 minutes."]},
{name:"Cheesy Bean Jacket Potato",category:"Budget",tags:["Vegetarian","Family"],time:65,cost:1.10,protein:18,calories:548,difficulty:"Idiot-proof",score:8.8,emoji:"🥔",blurb:"Crisp potato, molten cheese, beans. Britain survived on worse.",ingredients:["4 large baking potatoes","1 tbsp oil","800g baked beans","160g mature cheddar","2 spring onions"],steps:["Rub potatoes with oil and salt.","Bake at 210°C for 55–65 minutes until properly crisp, not anaemic.","Heat the beans and grate the cheese.","Split, fluff, load and finish with spring onion."]},
{name:"Chicken Stir Fry",category:"Quick",tags:["High Protein","Family"],time:22,cost:2.20,protein:42,calories:510,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.1,emoji:"🥡",blurb:"Faster than delivery and considerably less disappointing.",ingredients:["600g chicken breast, sliced","2 peppers","200g sugar snap peas","4 nests egg noodles","4 tbsp soy sauce","2 tbsp honey","1 tsp sesame oil"],steps:["Mix soy, honey and sesame oil.","Cook noodles and drain.","Stir-fry chicken on high heat for 6 minutes.","Add vegetables, then sauce and noodles. Toss hard for 3 minutes."]},
{name:"Air Fryer Chicken Kiev",category:"Air Fryer",tags:["High Protein","Fakeaway"],time:28,cost:2.48,protein:46,calories:585,difficulty:"Medium",score:9.5,emoji:"🔥",blurb:"Garlic butter stays inside if you stop stabbing it. Revolutionary.",verdict:"Crunchy armour, molten garlic butter and no sad frozen Kiev anywhere in sight.",ingredients:["4 chicken breasts","80g garlic butter","100g breadcrumbs","50g plain flour","2 eggs","oil spray"],steps:["Heat the air fryer to 190°C before you start. Warm circulating disappointment is not enough to crisp breadcrumbs.","Cut a deep pocket into the side of each chicken breast without slicing straight through. This is surgery, not a massacre.","Push cold garlic butter firmly into each pocket and pinch the opening shut. Leave gaps and the butter will make a break for freedom.","Season the flour, beat the eggs and spread the breadcrumbs onto separate plates. Congratulations, you have built a tiny production line.","Coat each breast in flour, then egg, then breadcrumbs, pressing firmly so the coating stays on the chicken instead of decorating the basket.","Chill for 15 minutes. Yes, wait. That short rest is what stops the whole thing falling apart like a cheap promise.","Spray lightly with oil and air fry for 18–22 minutes, turning once, until deeply golden and cooked through at the centre.","Rest for 3 minutes before cutting. The garlic butter inside is molten and has no concern whatsoever for your tongue."]},
{name:"Smoky Beef Chilli",category:"Budget",tags:["High Protein","Family"],time:55,cost:2.05,protein:41,calories:590,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.3,emoji:"🌶️",blurb:"Deep, smoky and built for a second helping you’ll pretend wasn’t planned.",ingredients:["500g lean beef mince","1 onion","2 garlic cloves","400g chopped tomatoes","400g kidney beans","2 tsp smoked paprika","1 tsp cumin"],steps:["Brown the mince until it actually has colour.","Add onion and garlic for 5 minutes.","Stir in spices, tomatoes and beans.","Simmer uncovered for 35 minutes. Taste, season, demolish."]},
{name:"Creamy Tuscan Chicken",category:"High Protein",tags:["Family","One Pan"],time:32,cost:2.75,protein:49,calories:620,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.6,emoji:"🍲",blurb:"Creamy, garlicky, suspiciously impressive for one pan.",ingredients:["600g chicken breast","200ml single cream","100g sun-dried tomatoes","150g spinach","3 garlic cloves","30g parmesan"],steps:["Sear chicken until golden and remove.","Cook garlic and tomatoes for 2 minutes.","Add cream and parmesan, then wilt in spinach.","Return chicken and simmer gently until cooked through."]},
{name:"Crispy Halloumi Fajitas",category:"Vegetarian",tags:["Quick","Fakeaway"],time:20,cost:2.30,protein:27,calories:640,difficulty:"Easy",score:8.9,emoji:"🌯",blurb:"Squeaky cheese, scorched peppers, zero sad salad energy.",ingredients:["450g halloumi","8 flour tortillas","3 peppers","1 red onion","2 tsp fajita seasoning","1 lime","salsa to serve"],steps:["Slice the peppers and onion into strips, not random geological formations.","Get the pan smoking hot, then char the vegetables until the edges catch.","Fry the halloumi separately until properly golden on both sides. Pale halloumi is rubber with ambitions.","Warm the tortillas, pile everything in, squeeze over lime and add salsa. Fold it before wearing it."]},
{name:"Pepperoni Pizza",category:"Fakeaway",tags:["Family","Fakeaway"],time:35,cost:2.05,protein:32,calories:710,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.3,emoji:"🍕",blurb:"Crisp base, molten cheese and enough pepperoni to make delivery apps nervous.",ingredients:["2 pizza bases","200g passata","250g mozzarella","120g pepperoni","1 tsp oregano","1 tbsp olive oil"],steps:["Heat the oven to 240°C with a tray inside. Pizza needs violence, not a gentle warm breeze.","Spread the passata thinly; drown the base and you’ll bake a wet doormat.","Scatter over mozzarella, pepperoni and oregano. Leave a border unless you enjoy scraping cheese off metal.","Slide onto the hot tray and bake for 10–12 minutes until blistered, crisp and shamelessly greasy."]},
{name:"Chicken Fajitas",category:"Fakeaway",tags:["Quick","High Protein"],time:24,cost:2.25,protein:44,calories:590,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.4,emoji:"🌯",blurb:"Sizzling chicken, scorched peppers and absolutely no limp takeaway nonsense.",ingredients:["600g chicken breast, sliced","8 flour tortillas","3 peppers, sliced","1 red onion","2 tsp fajita seasoning","1 lime","salsa"],steps:["Toss the chicken with seasoning and a slick of oil. Every strip gets coated; this isn’t a raffle.","Sear the chicken in a ripping-hot pan in batches so it browns instead of sweating sadly.","Char the peppers and onion for 5 minutes, then return the chicken and squeeze in the lime.","Warm the tortillas, load them hard and eat immediately while everything still has a pulse."]},
{name:"Beef Stroganoff",category:"Family",tags:["Quick","High Protein"],time:30,cost:2.85,protein:43,calories:640,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.5,emoji:"🥩",blurb:"Tender beef, mustardy mushroom sauce and no packet powder anywhere near it.",ingredients:["600g beef strips","300g mushrooms","1 onion","200ml soured cream","1 tbsp Dijon mustard","300g tagliatelle"],steps:["Boil the pasta in properly salted water. A timid pinch achieves nothing.","Sear the beef fast in batches, then get it out before it turns into boot leather.","Brown the mushrooms and onion, stir in mustard, then lower the heat before adding soured cream.","Return the beef for one minute, toss with pasta and serve. Do not boil the cream into oily rubble."]},
{name:"Beef Enchiladas",category:"Fakeaway",tags:["Family","Batch Cook"],time:45,cost:2.40,protein:39,calories:720,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.4,emoji:"🌮",blurb:"Saucy, cheesy, rolled-up carnage. Exactly what Tuesday deserved.",ingredients:["500g beef mince","8 tortillas","400g chopped tomatoes","1 onion","2 tsp cumin","180g cheddar","1 red chilli"],steps:["Brown the mince hard until you see dark, crispy bits. Grey mince is a cry for help.","Cook in the onion, chilli and cumin, then add half the tomatoes and simmer until thick.","Fill and roll the tortillas tightly. Arrange seam-side down so they don’t unravel like your plans.","Cover with remaining tomato and cheese; bake at 200°C for 20 minutes until furiously bubbling."]},
{name:"Beef Stew",category:"Family",tags:["Budget","Batch Cook"],time:120,cost:2.55,protein:42,calories:650,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.6,emoji:"🥘",blurb:"Dark gravy, collapsing beef and the sort of dinner weather was invented for.",verdict:"A proper bowl of slow-cooked comfort. No pastry lid, no identity crisis, just bloody good stew.",ingredients:["800g stewing beef","2 onions","3 carrots","500ml beef stock","2 tbsp flour","1 tbsp tomato purée","500g potatoes"],steps:["Heat the oven to 160°C and put a heavy casserole over high heat. Stew needs patience, but it still deserves a violent start.","Pat the beef dry, season it and dust it with flour. Wet meat steams, and grey cubes are no foundation for greatness.","Brown the beef in small batches until every side has a dark crust. Tip each batch onto a plate and stop overcrowding the bloody pot.","Lower the heat, add the onions and carrots and cook for 6–8 minutes until softened and catching at the edges.","Stir in the tomato purée and cook it for 2 minutes until brick-red. Raw purée tastes sharp and unfinished because it is.","Pour in the stock and scrape every sticky brown bit from the bottom. That is concentrated flavour, not washing-up residue.","Return the beef, add the potatoes, cover and cook for 90 minutes until the meat gives up when pressed with a fork.","Remove the lid for the final 20 minutes if the gravy looks thin, then rest for 10. Taste, season and serve in deep bowls—not under a bloody pie crust."]}
