const strongerSteps:Record<string,string[]>={
"One Pan Chicken & Rice":["Heat the oven to 190°C. Do it now; raw chicken has no interest in waiting for your oven to catch up.","Coat the chicken thighs with one teaspoon of smoked paprika, salt and black pepper, then brown them skin-side down for 5–6 minutes in an ovenproof pan.","Lift the chicken out. Fry the diced onion and sliced pepper in the same pan for 4 minutes, scraping up every sticky brown bit instead of washing the flavour away.","Stir in the rice and remaining paprika for one minute, then pour in the hot stock and bring it to a simmer.","Sit the chicken on top, skin facing up, and bake uncovered for 25 minutes. Bury it under the liquid and the skin will come out as limp as a wet sock.","Scatter in the peas and bake for another 5 minutes until the rice has absorbed the stock and the chicken is cooked through.","Rest for 5 minutes before serving. The rice finishes itself while you resist attacking the pan with a spoon."],
"Sausage Pasta Bake":["Heat the oven to 200°C and get a large pan of salted water boiling. Starting both late is how dinner ends up at bedtime.","Brown the sausages for 8 minutes, turning until properly coloured, then slice them into thick pieces.","Boil the penne for 2 minutes less than the packet says. It still has an oven sentence to serve, so stop trying to cook it twice.","Fry the onion for 5 minutes, add the garlic for 30 seconds, then pour in the passata and oregano and simmer for 8 minutes.","Stir in the sausage and drained pasta, season properly, then tip everything into a baking dish.","Cover with mozzarella and bake for 18–20 minutes until the top is bubbling and browned. Pale cheese is merely warm dairy.","Leave it alone for 5 minutes before serving unless you fancy removing the roof of your mouth."],
"Cheesy Bean Jacket Potato":["Heat the oven to 210°C. Prick the potatoes all over, because unexploded potatoes are easier to eat.","Rub them with oil and salt, place directly on the oven shelf and bake for 55–65 minutes until the skins are audibly crisp.","Warm the beans gently for 6–8 minutes. Do not boil them into orange wallpaper paste.","Grate the cheddar while the potatoes finish. This is not the moment for delicate little cheese shavings.","Split each potato, add a pinch of salt and fluff the middle hard with a fork before loading in the beans.","Bury the lot under cheddar and return to the oven for 4 minutes until melted.","Finish with spring onions and serve immediately while the skin still has some backbone."],
"Chicken Stir Fry":["Mix the soy sauce, honey and sesame oil in a mug before the pan gets hot. Stir-fries move quickly; frantic cupboard hunting does not count as cooking.","Boil the noodles for one minute less than the packet says, drain them and rinse briefly under cold water so they stop cooking.","Heat a wok until properly smoking, add a splash of oil and sear the sliced chicken for 5–6 minutes until golden and cooked through.","Add the peppers and sugar snap peas and stir-fry for 3 minutes. They need crunch, not a full emotional collapse.","Tip in the noodles and sauce, then toss hard over high heat for 90 seconds until everything is glossy.","Taste before serving. If it needs more soy, add it now instead of quietly accepting bland noodles."],
"Smoky Beef Chilli":["Put a heavy pan over high heat and brown the beef mince in batches. Grey steamed mince is not the deep smoky start we need.","Lower the heat, add the diced onion and cook for 6 minutes before adding the garlic for another minute.","Stir in the paprika and cumin for 30 seconds until fragrant. Raw spices taste like the dusty back of a cupboard.","Add the chopped tomatoes and a half-tin of water, scraping the bottom of the pan clean.","Drain the kidney beans, stir them in and simmer uncovered for 35 minutes, stirring occasionally until thick enough to sit on a spoon.","Taste, season with salt and black pepper, then give it another 5 minutes. Chilli rewards patience and punishes watery shortcuts."],
"Creamy Tuscan Chicken":["Season the chicken and sear it in a wide hot pan for 5 minutes per side until golden, then move it to a plate.","Lower the heat and fry the garlic and chopped sun-dried tomatoes for one minute. Burn the garlic now and the whole sauce tastes bitter.","Pour in the cream, add the parmesan and stir gently until smooth. Keep it below a boil unless greasy rubble was the plan.","Wilt in the spinach a handful at a time instead of trying to force the entire bag under one spoon.","Return the chicken and any resting juices, then simmer gently for 8–10 minutes until the centre is cooked through.","Taste the sauce, add black pepper and only then decide whether it needs salt—the parmesan has already turned up with plenty."],
"Crispy Halloumi Fajitas":["Slice the peppers and onion into even strips, not random geological formations.","Get a heavy pan screaming hot, add a little oil and char the vegetables for 5–6 minutes so the edges catch while the middle keeps some bite.","Toss the halloumi with fajita seasoning and fry it in a separate dry pan for 2 minutes per side until properly golden.","Warm each tortilla for 20 seconds so it folds instead of cracking like old paint.","Pile in the vegetables and halloumi, squeeze over lime and add salsa without flooding the thing.","Fold the sides in and roll tightly. A loose fajita has one ambition: decorating your trousers."],
"Pepperoni Pizza":["Heat the oven to 240°C with a heavy baking tray inside for at least 20 minutes. Pizza needs fierce heat, not positive thinking.","Spread passata thinly over each base, leaving a 2cm border. Too much sauce turns the middle into a wet doormat.","Tear over the mozzarella, add the pepperoni and finish with oregano and a light drizzle of oil.","Slide the pizzas onto the hot tray and bake for 10–12 minutes until the crust is crisp and the cheese is blistered.","Rest for 2 minutes before slicing. Molten cheese has no concern for the roof of your mouth.","Cut into wedges and serve while the base still snaps instead of folding sadly."],
"Chicken Fajitas":["Toss the sliced chicken with fajita seasoning, salt and a tablespoon of oil until every strip is coated. This is not a seasoning raffle.","Heat a large pan until smoking and sear the chicken in two batches for 5–6 minutes each so it browns instead of sweating.","Remove the chicken, then char the peppers and onion in the same pan for 5 minutes.","Return the chicken, squeeze in the lime and toss for one minute until everything is hot and glossy.","Warm the tortillas for 20 seconds each. Cold tortillas split, then dinner ends up in your lap.","Load with chicken, peppers and salsa, fold tightly and eat immediately while the pan is still hissing."],
"Beef Stroganoff":["Get the tagliatelle into properly salted boiling water and cook until just al dente. Keep a mug of the pasta water before draining.","Heat a wide pan until very hot and sear the beef in batches for 60–90 seconds per side, then remove it before it becomes boot leather.","Brown the mushrooms for 5 minutes without constantly poking them, then add the onion and cook for another 4 minutes.","Stir in the mustard, lower the heat and add the soured cream. Do not boil it unless split sauce excites you.","Return the beef for one minute, loosen with a splash of pasta water and season with black pepper.","Toss through the tagliatelle and serve immediately. Stroganoff waits for nobody."],
"Beef Enchiladas":["Heat the oven to 200°C and brown the mince hard for 7–8 minutes until dark crispy bits appear.","Add the onion, chilli and cumin and cook for 5 minutes before stirring in half the chopped tomatoes.","Simmer for 10 minutes until thick. Watery filling makes soggy enchiladas and nobody asked for a tortilla bath.","Divide the beef between the tortillas, roll them tightly and place seam-side down in a baking dish.","Spoon over the remaining tomatoes, cover with cheddar and bake for 20 minutes until furiously bubbling.","Rest for 5 minutes before serving so the filling stays inside the enchiladas instead of escaping across the plate."]};
